{"id": "EUVD-2026-102955", "enisaUuid": "50a98c5b-0b24-3a54-abfe-2376bc051c92", "description": "Safing Portmaster before 2.2.5 contains a missing authorization vulnerability that allows unprivileged local processes to force updates by calling the POST /api/v1/updates/from-url endpoint registered with api.PermitAnyone. Attackers can supply an attacker-controlled index URL that bypasses version checks and auto-apply settings, installing older Safing-signed releases carrying previously fixed vulnerabilities.", "datePublished": "2026-10-16T17:39:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T20:58:29", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/safing/portmaster/issues/2292", "https://github.com/safing/portmaster/blob/v2.2.3/service/core/api.go#L145-L159", "https://github.com/safing/portmaster/commit/f943e1eaf98f45bc48490bf288e1d63c04929ae0", "https://github.com/safing/portmaster/releases/tag/v2.2.5", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/safing-portmaster-before-2.2.5-unauthenticated-forced-downgrade-via-api-v1-updates-from-url"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111664", "GHSA-6952-c35h-6rff"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cf5a51f4-d357-39b5-b412-953d9bfe52cb", "product": {"name": "portmaster", "vendor": {"name": "safing"}}, "product_version": "0 <2.2.5"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5bbf17f2-1427-35bb-a9f3-8b511dc57b15", "vendor": {"name": "safing"}}], "isExploited": false}